# PHANTOM — Real-World Cybersecurity Gap Analysis
> Cross-referenced against: NahamSec Resources, PayloadsAllTheThings (79k ⭐), Galaxy Bug Bounty Checklist, OSCP/PNPT methodology, HackerOne top hackers, Red Team operator playbooks
> Last updated: 2026-07-30

---

## ✅ What PHANTOM Already Has (Strengths)

PHANTOM is ahead of most open-source frameworks in these areas:

| Category | Tool(s) | Coverage |
|---|---|---|
| Port Scanning | `nmap`, `masscan`, `rustscan` | ✅ Excellent |
| Subdomain Enum | `subfinder`, `amass` | ✅ Excellent |
| Web Crawling | `katana`, `hakrawler` | ✅ Excellent |
| HTTP Probing | `httpx` | ✅ Excellent |
| Web Fuzzing | `ffuf`, `feroxbuster`, `dirsearch`, `gobuster`, `dirb` | ✅ Excellent |
| Vuln Scanning | `nuclei` (3000+ templates) | ✅ Excellent |
| XSS Scanning | `dalfox` | ✅ Good |
| SQL Injection | `sqlmap` | ✅ Good |
| Parameter Discovery | `paramspider`, `arjun`, `x8` | ✅ Good |
| Password Cracking | `hydra`, `hashcat`, `john` | ✅ Good |
| Binary Analysis | `ghidra`, `radare2`, `gdb`, `angr` | ✅ Good |
| Exploitation | `metasploit`, `msfvenom` | ✅ Good |
| OSINT (Passive) | `subfinder`, `amass` | ⚠️ Partial |
| Reporting | Jinja2 templates | ⚠️ Basic |

